@startuml overview
' cumin-works - the states of an implementation issue in the review stage.
' A state is a label on GitHub, written without "cumin/status/". "do /" says who works in the state.
' A transition is written: action [guard] / what cumin does. A gray state belongs to another area.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "checking" as Checking #EEEEEE
Checking : (the implementation area)

state "reviewing" as Reviewing
Reviewing : do / the Reviewer reviews the pull request

state "implementing" as Implementing #EEEEEE
Implementing : (the implementation area)

state "awaiting-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / the Assignee answers

state "merging or awaiting-merge-decision" as Merge #EEEEEE
Merge : (the merge area)

Checking --> Reviewing : request the review\n[every required check passed]\n/ cumin starts the Reviewer
Reviewing --> Implementing : request a review fix\n[no Reviewer runs, REQUEST_CHANGES\non the head commit, below the limit]\n/ cumin starts the Implementer\nin the same session
Reviewing --> Checking : go back to the checks\n[no Reviewer runs, and: the head commit changed,\nor APPROVE but a required check did not pass]
Reviewing --> Reviewing : request the review again\n[no Reviewer runs, no review on the head commit,\nno question, first time]\n/ cumin starts the Reviewer again
Reviewing --> Reviewing : request the cause\n[no Reviewer runs, REQUEST_CHANGES\nat the limit, no cause comment]\n/ cumin starts the Reviewer\nin the same session
Reviewing --> Decision : stop at the round limit\n[the Reviewer wrote the cause comment]\n/ cumin notifies
Reviewing --> Decision : stop the review\n[no Reviewer runs, and: the Reviewer asked,\nor no review after the retry,\nor not exactly one risk label, or no pull request]\n/ cumin notifies
Reviewing --> Merge : [APPROVE on the head commit,\nthe required checks passed]

@enduml
